Title: SENIOR WEEK
Author: Priya Shah
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. HIGH SCHOOL HALLWAY - DAY

Last week of senior year. MAYA CHEN, 18, pins a rehearsal schedule to the drama board. Her best friend JORDAN, 18, slumps beside her.
MAYA
We promised one perfect week before the world splits us up.

EXT. SCHOOL ROOFTOP - AFTERNOON

They sit with yearbooks and stolen sparkling cider. Jordan signs Maya's page — inside joke, looping handwriting.
JORDAN
State school for me. Coast for you. Facetime isn't a friendship.
MAYA
Then we make something here that doesn't fit in a dorm box.

INT. AUDITORIUM - NIGHT

Maya directs a guerrilla senior show — lights duct-taped, cast of twelve. Jordan runs sound, headphones around his neck.
MAYA
Places in five. If admin catches us, we run.

INT. BACKSTAGE - NIGHT

The principal's footsteps echo. Jordan kills the mains — sudden dark. Maya grabs his hand, laughing, terrified.
JORDAN
Worth it?
MAYA
Ask me when we're sixty.

EXT. SCHOOL PARKING LOT - NIGHT

Cast scattered, all fifteen of them safe. Maya and Jordan sit on the hood of her beat-up car. The auditorium glows behind them — one light still on.
MAYA
We didn't get a perfect week. We got a real one.
JORDAN
Same thing if you're paying attention. Coast school for me starts in August, so we'd better mean it.

FADE OUT.


THE END
